      "text": "Explain the trend in reactivity in Group 1 in terms of electronic configurations. The elements in Group 1 of the Periodic Table are called the alkali metals. The group contains the elements shown in Figure 11.3. Francium (pronounced france-ee-um), at the bottom of the group, is radioactive. One of its isotopes is produced during the radioactive decay of uranium-235, but is extremely short-lived. At any one time scientists estimate that there is only about 20-30g of francium present in the whole of the Earth's crust and no one has ever seen a piece of francium. When you know about the rest of Group 1 you can predict what francium would be like. We will make those predictions later.",
